From: OpenHarmonyPCDeveloper adaptation <nobody@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 9/10] Stop linking gomp: the OpenMP-enabled in-tree libdivsufsort is gone

Part of the RapMap 0.15.0 adaptation for HarmonyOS PC (aarch64).
Generated against upstream tag salmon-v0.15.0.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -117,7 +117,16 @@
 set( BOOST_EXTRA_FLAGS "--layout=tagged" )
 ## this get's set differently below if we
 ## are on clang & apple
-set (NON_APPLECLANG_LIBS gomp)
+## Upstream linked gomp because its in-tree libdivsufsort ExternalProject
+## was configured with -DUSE_OPENMP=TRUE.  Patch 0001 consumes the Conan
+## libdivsufsort package instead, whose exported cpp_info carries no OpenMP
+## requirement, and no translation unit here uses an OpenMP directive
+## (grep -rn '#pragma omp|omp_get|_OPENMP' over src/ include/ finds
+## nothing), so there is nothing left for this library to satisfy.  Only
+## APPLE cleared the list, so clang everywhere else still asked the linker
+## for -lgomp, which the OHOS clang sysroot does not ship (LLVM provides
+## libomp instead): ld.lld reports 'unable to find library -lgomp'.
+set (NON_APPLECLANG_LIBS "")
 set (PTHREAD_LIB)
 
 if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
